    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n22080" root="شرح" body-key="$">
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">شُرَيْحٌ</span></b>  The <i>vulva of a woman;</i> (O, K;) and
(K) so ↓ <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مَشْرَحٌ</span></b> : (A, Mgh, K:) or a proper name
for <i>the vulva of a woman;</i> like as <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">رُمَيْحٌ</span> is a
proper name for “ the penis. ” (TA in art. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">رمح</span>.
[Golius appears to have found in the K <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">الحَرُّ</span> in
the place of <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">الحِرُ</span>.])

